libvgcode: make the OpenGL ES variant work on phones

OrcaSlicer builds libvgcode only for desktop OpenGL, and its OpenGL ES variant
(also in PrusaSlicer 2.9.0, where it served WebGL) is broken on Android in
OrcaSlicer 2.4.2 and in its main branch as of 2026-09:

- It does not compile: the vertex data was changed to four floats per vertex
  for GL_RGBA32F (SPE-2411), but the OpenGL ES textures still take three.
  TextureData now takes four floats and uploads them as GL_RGBA32F, as
  PrusaSlicer did when it fixed the same code.
- The vertex shaders read the textures through lowp samplers: sampler2D has
  no precision of its own, which GLSL ES makes lowp in vertex shaders, and
  usampler2D is declared lowp. Mobile GPUs honour that, so colours, which are
  packed into floats up to 16777215, overflow and every toolpath turns white,
  and segment indices would stop at 65535. Both samplers are highp now.
- Every segment is drawn as 24 vertices, which the vertex shader places by
  their corner id alone, so it shades each of the eight corners three times.
  A tile-based mobile GPU keeps every shaded vertex of a frame in memory,
  over a gigabyte for a print of a million and a half segments, and does not
  draw the frame at all. SegmentTemplate draws the triangles by index from
  the eight corners: the same picture, with a third of the shading.

Applied by engine/CMakeLists.txt to a copy of src/libvgcode in the build tree;
the submodule is not modified. Remove it once upstream has these fixes.

